      players: 'Two or more players; Scarne describes it as best for about six. One player is the banker (dealer). The first banker is chosen by dealing cards one at a time until an Ace appears; the turn to be banker passes to the right after each deal. Each player may accept one case card from the dealer to bet on, or refuse; the dealer also holds one card. Cards are revealed one by one from a dealing box or shoe.',
      deck: '52 cards (or Shoe of 6 decks).',
